#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.tools.capturable:2
msgid ""
"Decorator that specifies that a callable alias should be run with capturing. "
"This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.completer:2
msgid "Decorator that attaches a completer function to an alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.completer:4
msgid "Usage::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.completer:6
msgid ""
"def _my_completer(command, alias):\n"
"    return {'opt1', 'opt2'}\n"
"\n"
"@aliases.register\n"
"@aliases.completer(_my_completer)\n"
"def _hello(args):\n"
"    echo @(args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.completer:14
msgid "Now ``hello <TAB>`` will suggest ``opt1`` and ``opt2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.aliases.Aliases.return_command:2
msgid ""
"Decorator that switches alias from returning result to return in new command "
"for execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.tools.threadable:2
msgid ""
"Decorator that specifies that a callable alias should be run in a background "
"thread. This is the default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.tools.uncapturable:2
msgid ""
"Decorator that specifies that a callable alias should not be run with any "
"capturing. This is often needed if the alias call interactive subprocess, "
"like pagers and text editors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.tools.unthreadable:2
msgid ""
"Decorator that specifies that a callable alias should be run only on the "
"main thread process. This is often needed for debuggers and profilers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.eval_alias:2
msgid ""
"\"Evaluates\" the alias ``value``, by recursively looking up the leftmost "
"token and \"expanding\" if it's also an alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.eval_alias:5
msgid ""
"A value like ``[\"cmd\", \"arg\"]`` might transform like this: ``> [\"cmd\", "
"\"arg\"] -> [\"ls\", \"-al\", \"arg\"] -> callable()`` where ``cmd=ls -al`` "
"and ``ls`` is an alias with its value being a callable.  The resulting "
"callable will be \"partially applied\" with ``[\"-al\", \"arg\"]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.aliases.Aliases.eval_alias:11
msgid ""
"``env_out``, if given, is a mutable dict that accumulates the env overlay "
"requested by any ``return_command`` alias encountered while resolving the "
"chain (via dict-return ``\"env\"`` key). The top-level :meth:`get` caller "
"passes its own collector dict here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.aliases.Aliases.expand_alias:2
msgid ""
"Expands any aliases present in line if alias does not point to a builtin "
"function and if alias is only a single command. The command won't be "
"expanded if the cursor's inside/behind it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get:2
msgid ""
"Returns list that represent command with resolved aliases. The ``key`` can "
"be string with alias name or list for a command. In the first position will "
"be the resolved command name or callable alias. If the key is not present, "
"then `default` is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get:7
msgid ""
"``decorators`` is the list of `DecoratorAlias` objects that found during "
"resolving aliases (#5443)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get:10
msgid ""
"Note! The return value is always list because during resolving we can find "
"return_command alias that can completely replace command and add new "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:2
msgid "Return the cleaned docstring of an alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:4
msgid "Resolution order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:6
msgid ""
"An explicit doc set via the dict-form ``aliases[k] = {\"alias\": ..., "
"\"doc\": \"...\"}`` takes priority over everything else — it's the only way "
"to attach a description to a list/string alias and an intentional override "
"for callable aliases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:11
msgid ""
"For ``FuncAlias`` instances, the wrapped function's ``__doc__`` (read from "
"``alias.func`` directly to avoid falling back to ``FuncAlias.__doc__``, "
"which would otherwise leak the class placeholder ``\"Provides a callable "
"alias for xonsh commands.\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:16
msgid ""
"For any other alias object (e.g. ``ArgParserAlias``, ``ExecAlias``), the "
"object's own ``__doc__``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:18
msgid "List- and string-aliases without an explicit doc yield ``\"\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/aliases.py:docstring of xonsh.aliases.Aliases.get_doc:20
msgid ""
"The returned string is run through :func:`inspect.cleandoc` so multi-line "
"docstrings have shared indentation removed."
msgstr ""

